atos al límite se distribuyen según criterios de eficiencia o de acceso a recursos.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 57 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 5.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 11.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 6.8 to 18.2. December accounts for 9% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,950 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio shows a pattern, but it doesn't prove misconduct. Prices might be close to the limit due to market conditions. Budgets or needs could also explain the numbers without any wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for unusual patterns. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same need. Look at contract [1] to see what was purchased and if it aligns with the body's stated goals.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["XI11HFsQLXpWhbmkna2nXQ%3D%3D","2GdAIo1bRNFt5r0ngvMetA%3D%3D","%2FSiAnqjPZWgaF6cS8TCh%2FA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}